jobs.description:
The Tractebel Business Area Gas, Energy \& Nuclear is looking for a Medior Engineer in Radiological Characterisation to join its Radiation Protection, Radwaste and Decommissioning Competence Centre.  



This Competence Centre is responsible for all engineering aspects in the field of:


* Radiation Protection;
* Radiation Monitoring;
* Radiological Characterisation;
* Radioactive Waste Management (operational and dismantling waste);
* Decommissioning Concepts (tools, techniques, conceptual design studies…).



Within this structure, the Radiological Characterisation team is responsible for:


* The radiological characterisation of building, structure and equipment in a nuclear installation through measurements, sampling campaigns, simulations and calculations;
* The final radiological characterisation of waste produced during operation, post\-operation and dismantling phases of nuclear installation, including:

* The set up of strategies for the characterisation processes


* The selection and procurement of measurement systems


* The realization of theoretical and/or numerical and/or empirical studies


* The definition of scaling factors and methodology.




The team delivers high\-level engineering and consultancy services to Electrabel as well as other national and international clients. The team works closely with other Competence Centers, the project managers, the Client, the safety authorities and the radioactive waste management agencies.  



Because of the strong increase of the business activity, we are looking for motivated Engineers to contribute in our day\-to\-day challenges as well as in our long\-term objectives.




**What we offer**



* Tractebel is more than a place to work. It’s your chance to evolve alongside top experts on impactful projects around the world. It’s an environment built on team spirit, where you can reach your highest potential.
* We actively support the development of our people, and the opportunities for growth within the ENGIE Group are wide open.
* We offer a competitive salary package including representation allowances, double paid holidays, meal vouchers, eco cheques, bonuses, hospitalization insurance, PC purchase plan, ENGIE stock options, and more.
* Our mobility plans are customizable to your needs, including a company car, train pass, bike lease, or combinations thereof. You can also swap your company car for the flexible and tax\-friendly Belgian Mobility Budget!
* Flexible, hybrid arrangements enable working from home (2 days per week), on\-site or on the go or even part time. Tractebel participates in your home office expenses, through advantageous purchase programs and generous contributions to your internet and mobile plans.
* Holidays: 32 days with opportunity to buy 5 extra days.
* To celebrate our successes, and just have fun, we get together for team sports, afterworks, team \-building activities, our annual party, and more.



**Your key responsibilities**





As Radiological Characterisation Engineer, you are responsible for the successful delivery of the projects, tasks and studies entrusted to you.  



In close collaboration with your colleagues and your team leader, you act as an interface between on\-site activities at Tihange nuclear power plant and Competence Center, ensuring alignment between field and office work.  



You contribute to the development of characterisation programmes, perform engineering studies and ensure proper follow\-up of projects.  



To maintain close interaction with field teams, you will work up to 3 days per week on the Tihange site.  



Your responsibilities are:



* Conducting radiological characterisation studies in line with the expectations of the Client and the radioactive Waste Management Agencies;
* Monitor and support the operation of gamma spectrometry and dose rate measurement equipment, while progressively developing strong technical expertise in this field in order to support clients’ activities;
* Developing and applying capabilities with computer codes such as MicroShield, MCNP or RayXpert but also in\-house Python calculation codes and data treatments tools;
* Writing technical specifications and follow\-up of orders for the procurement of measurement systems and radiological campaigns;
* Develop and maintain a strong expertise in radiological characterisation, based on national and international references, standards and practices;
* Share your knowledge and experiences with Clients and colleagues to ensure alignment concerning the work to be realized and setting the right expectations;
* Delivering ‘quality on time’: in order to achieve this objective, you will get all support required in terms of technical training, coaching and availability of (IT) resources;
* Verifying work performed by your colleagues guaranteeing the expected high quality level;
* Correctly applying the Integrated Management System (IMS) procedures;
* Providing regular feedback concerning ongoing activities to your team leader and your hierarchy, while working autonomously towards the goals defined for you;
* Identifying and implementing possible synergies with other teams and/or competence centers;
* Contributing to the preparation of technical bids;
* Providing (internal) presentations and trainings;
* Participating actively to regular meetings with your colleagues during which workload, technical issues, project follow\-up, development strategy and transversal activity coordination are discussed.
* You will collaborate actively with your colleagues from Project Management and Competence Centre departments and build a close relationship while working for the same goal, actively developing cross department projects for your Clients.
* You act as an ambassador of Tractebel and the ENGIE Group values (Ethics, QHSE,…) in all your contacts, both inside and outside the ENGIE group, and other external stakeholders.




**We would love to hear from people with**




* You have the drive to become a technical expert in this field;
* You hold a master’s degree or PhD in engineering or sciences (preferably in physics);
* You have experience (at least 5 years) in the nuclear sector;
* You are fluent in French and in English (Dutch in an asset);
* You can draw up reports in French and in English;
* You are willing to work on the Tihange site up to 3 days per week;
* You are flexible and creative in finding technical solutions;
* You combine autonomy with strong team spirit;
* You are open to gain new competencies as well as to share them;
* You are comfortable with IT tools (MS Office); knowledge of Python is an advantage.




**Our Recruitment Process**




* Pre\-screener conversation / HR in\-depth interview on\-site / in teams with the Talent Acquisition Partner
* Final business interview on\-site with your future manager


Research shows that men apply when they meet 60% of the requirements while women only apply when they are convinced they meet 100%. Don’t let that hold you back – we’d love to hear from you!




**Who we are**





Ready to engineer your positive impact? Then join Tractebel, part of the ENGIE Group, and our 5,000 passionate experts around the globe, driven by shaping a more sustainable world every day. Make your contribution to carbon neutrality in markets like nuclear, renewables, power \& gas, electrical grids, hydropower \& dams, water resources \& supply, desalination, complex \& high\-tech buildings, transport infrastructures, and ports \& waterways.  

Our top priorities are people, ethics, safety, and sustainability. With Tractebel, you are uniquely positioned to make a positive impact on global net\-zero targets. The driving force behind reaching these goals is our greatest asset: you. Our people come first, and our strength is in our diversity. Because diversity leads to fresh perspectives that drive performance and innovation, we welcome all applicants and remain committed to an inclusive workplace.  

Find out more about Tractebel, our activities and why you should join us here!  

At ENGIE, every talent has a role to play in accelerating the energy transition. Make a difference and enjoy a fulfilling professional experience. Take on exciting challenges and build a career path that reflects who you are. Join us and be part of the adventure of the century!


